From 920f3f23ac45a7c7f4606ade167771df7f7643e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:50:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] gateway: no per-request stat/realpath on the event
 loop; scratch GC off the board lock

laptop-1's gateway logged 288 event-loop stalls in an hour (1269 s), ~10/min while
`hermes kanban gc` removed scratch workspaces. Outside the plugin discovery lock (PR #1923),
the leaf frames were per-request filesystem calls on the loop, and Desktop session-ticket
bootstraps queued behind them for 25-45 s.

- Plugin consent gate: `_get_dashboard_plugins` stat'ed every plugin dir (~80) on every
  /api/plugins/* HTTP and WS request. The sweep now runs at most once per
  DASHBOARD_PLUGINS_STALE_CHECK_SECS (5 s), and `_plugin_api_request_refused` reads the cached
  list only (`_fresh_dashboard_plugins`), sending a due sweep or rescan to a worker thread.
  A secondary profile's list gets the same window.
- `_config_profile_scope` compares homes with the memoized `hermes_home_key`, and
  `get_secret_source_values` / hydration use a memoized home key (`env_loader._home_key`;
  existing homes only, as hermes_home_key does). `_is_process_home` uses hermes_home_key too.
- Control socket `_posix_peer_subject`: the home's "no symlinked component" realpath verdict
  is reused for 30 s (passes only). The home is still lstat'ed per connection, so it turning
  into a symlink or changing owner/mode is refused at once.
- `gc_task_scratch` holds the board write lock only for the candidate SELECT. The inventory,
  walks and rmtree run outside it; each removal re-checks the owner (unchanged path and
  completion, terminal, no active children, no live sharer or job) in a short txn and detaches
  the tree by rename there, then removes the detached copy unlocked.

Tests (RED on base: 10 failures; GREEN 12/12):
tests/hermes_cli/test_loop_fs_request_paths.py,
tests/gateway/test_control_socket_peer_realpath_cache.py,
tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_scratch_gc_lock_scope.py.
Every test file referencing the changed functions (98 files, 1739 tests) passes.

Left on request paths (not changed here): serve_css / serve_spa static handlers
(is_file/resolve/read_text per asset request), `load_config_readonly`'s per-call config stat
in the consent gate, `load_env_file` / managed .env reads in `build_profile_secret_scope`
per scoped request, `home_mode_unsafe`'s ACL/getpwall probe when the home is group-writable,
and the secondary-profile `plugin_api_path` resolve in `in_process_router_refused`.

